WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.480 --> 00:00:05.160
Zooey Deschanel has brought her humor, charm,
and vocal stylings to both the big and small

00:00:05.160 --> 00:00:05.660
screens.

00:00:05.880 --> 00:00:08.440
Now, there seems to be very little on the
horizon for her.

00:00:09.120 --> 00:00:12.160
So why aren't we seeing more of one of Hollywood's
most likable stars?

00:00:12.820 --> 00:00:17.440
Zooey Deschanel might not be popping up on
your TV screen as much as she used to because,

00:00:17.440 --> 00:00:19.720
let's face it, she could really use some time
off.

00:00:20.369 --> 00:00:24.300
She's been acting consistently since her teen
years, when she broke out in the late '90s

00:00:24.310 --> 00:00:29.359
and early 2000s with roles in films like Mumford
and Almost Famous, along with an appearance

00:00:29.360 --> 00:00:30.460
in an Offspring video.

00:00:31.080 --> 00:00:32.439
Remember the Offspring?

00:00:32.680 --> 00:00:35.140
Yeah, she's been doing this acting thing for
a while.

00:00:35.540 --> 00:00:39.539
Over the last couple of decades, Deschanel
has appeared in dozens of movies large and

00:00:39.540 --> 00:00:42.460
small and provided voice work for animated
projects.

00:00:42.860 --> 00:00:47.510
All that, plus she starred in more than 100
episodes across seven seasons of the single-camera

00:00:47.510 --> 00:00:48.380
comedy New Girl.

00:00:48.980 --> 00:00:53.160
Deschanel even served as a producer on the
project and co-wrote and performed the theme

00:00:53.160 --> 00:00:53.660
song.

00:00:54.000 --> 00:00:56.360
In short, she's probably a little tired.

00:00:56.720 --> 00:01:01.260
She's earned her hiatus and won't likely miss
the grind of a 22-episode TV season for a

00:01:01.260 --> 00:01:01.760
while.

00:01:02.400 --> 00:01:06.900
Zooey Deschanel rose to fame by portraying
a movie character archetype that soon turned

00:01:06.900 --> 00:01:08.820
into a trite character cliché.

00:01:09.100 --> 00:01:13.860
Film writer Nathan Rabin coined the term "Manic
Pixie Dream Girl" to describe Kirsten Dunst's

00:01:13.860 --> 00:01:17.880
character in the 2005 movie Elizabethtown,
a young woman who, quote...

00:01:18.420 --> 00:01:23.050
"...exists solely in the fevered imaginations
of sensitive writer-directors to teach broodingly

00:01:23.050 --> 00:01:26.920
soulful young men to embrace life and its
infinite mysteries and adventures."

00:01:27.360 --> 00:01:31.310
Sounds a lot like the roles Deschanel played
in (500) Days of Summer, The Hitchhiker's

00:01:31.310 --> 00:01:33.600
Guide to the Galaxy, and Yes Man, huh?

00:01:33.600 --> 00:01:35.420
"How did I not see this before?!"

00:01:35.420 --> 00:01:39.920
Deschanel is regularly identified with this
concept, and the death of its popularity could

00:01:39.920 --> 00:01:41.440
hurt her chances to get cast.

00:01:41.850 --> 00:01:46.200
She's also nearing 40, a little too old to
be playing "girls," and she's honestly too

00:01:46.210 --> 00:01:48.920
accomplished a performer to play such thankless
roles anymore.

00:01:50.210 --> 00:01:54.180
With New Girl taking up most of her time,
Zooey Deschanel hasn't appeared in all that

00:01:54.180 --> 00:01:56.520
many major movies in the 2010s.

00:01:56.880 --> 00:02:01.420
She only co-starred in two big live-action
outings during that time: the medieval comedy

00:02:01.420 --> 00:02:04.960
Your Highness and the music industry satire
Rock the Kasbah.

00:02:04.960 --> 00:02:08.740
Not only did both movies flop, but they flopped
spectacularly.

00:02:09.060 --> 00:02:13.620
Deschanel played the "damsel in distress"
in Your Highness, a swords-and-sorcery stoner

00:02:13.620 --> 00:02:17.460
adventure, alongside Natalie Portman, James
Franco, and Danny McBride.

00:02:17.860 --> 00:02:23.120
It earned a disappointing $21 million, less
than half of its $50 million budget.

00:02:23.460 --> 00:02:28.700
Meanwhile, Forbes named Rock the Kasbah the
biggest flop of 2015, for both commercial

00:02:28.700 --> 00:02:30.100
and critical reasons.

00:02:30.260 --> 00:02:34.720
It grossed about $3 million against a $15
million production budget.

00:02:34.900 --> 00:02:39.820
Film reviewers hated it, too: it's cursed
with an abysmal 8% rating on Rotten Tomatoes.

00:02:40.020 --> 00:02:40.820
"Hah!

00:02:41.620 --> 00:02:42.120
Bleh!

00:02:42.240 --> 00:02:43.020
Heh heh.

00:02:43.180 --> 00:02:43.700
BURRR.

00:02:43.800 --> 00:02:45.480
No, that's crazy.

00:02:45.700 --> 00:02:46.760
That ain't real!

00:02:47.480 --> 00:02:48.480
That's dumb."

00:02:48.580 --> 00:02:53.260
After a string of unsuccessful movies, Deschanel
might be a bit iffy about returning to the

00:02:53.260 --> 00:02:54.780
big-screen, and we can't blame her.

00:02:55.140 --> 00:02:57.340
After all, the talent's not always at fault!

00:02:57.840 --> 00:02:58.940
Which might be why…

00:02:59.720 --> 00:03:03.680
After starring on her own show for the better
part of a decade, Deschanel just might have

00:03:03.680 --> 00:03:08.180
lost interest in playing supporting roles
in the big-budget, high-profile, commercially-minded

00:03:08.180 --> 00:03:10.060
movies that made her a household name.

00:03:10.420 --> 00:03:13.780
Instead, she might just return to smaller,
more intimate films.

00:03:14.220 --> 00:03:19.769
Her performance in the low-key 2003 romantic
drama All the Real Girls won Deschanel nominations

00:03:19.769 --> 00:03:20.640
and awards.

00:03:21.090 --> 00:03:26.040
That set the tone for bankable movie and TV
star Deschanel's parallel career as an indie

00:03:26.040 --> 00:03:30.139
stalwart, with roles in well-received and
thoughtful fare such as Winter Passing, Our

00:03:30.140 --> 00:03:33.020
Idiot Brother, Gigantic, and The Driftless
Area.

00:03:33.220 --> 00:03:36.980
It's a safe bet that the next time we see
her in a feature film, it might be a festival

00:03:36.980 --> 00:03:41.100
entry or some hidden gem deep within Netflix's
"independent drama" category.

00:03:42.120 --> 00:03:47.400
Zooey Deschanel may have had a hard time scheduling
acting gigs in 2013 because her side career

00:03:47.400 --> 00:03:49.300
as a musician was so successful.

00:03:49.569 --> 00:03:54.840
While filming the 2007 movie The Go-Getter,
star Deschanel met major indie music figure

00:03:54.840 --> 00:03:55.420
M. Ward.

00:03:55.880 --> 00:03:59.900
She acted, he did the soundtrack, and the
director thought they ought to record a duet

00:03:59.900 --> 00:04:00.400
together.

00:04:00.400 --> 00:04:03.080
They did, and their band was off and running.

00:04:03.280 --> 00:04:08.180
A little bit folk, a little bit classic country,
She &amp; Him play whimsical pop music, with Ward

00:04:08.180 --> 00:04:11.220
handling the guitar work and Deschanel taking
the lead vocals.

00:04:11.500 --> 00:04:16.280
Since 2009, they've released six albums of
mostly original music, plus two Christmas

00:04:16.280 --> 00:04:18.040
records and a covers collection.

00:04:18.360 --> 00:04:21.940
They've had some success with their singles
"In the Sun" and "Thieves," and they play

00:04:21.940 --> 00:04:24.200
a lot of super-chill music festivals each
summer.

00:04:24.460 --> 00:04:28.740
Deschanel just can't be delighting fans with
movies when she's up there on stage warbling

00:04:28.740 --> 00:04:30.740
adorable, old-fashioned love songs.

00:04:31.280 --> 00:04:33.100
But, hey, we'll take what we can get!

